H3000.definition:
from H1288 (בָרַךְ) and H3050 (יָהּ); blessed of Jah;
Jeberekjah, an Israelite
KJV: Jeberechiah.

H3001.definition:
a primitive root;
to be ashamed, confused or disappointed; also (as failing) to dry up (as water) or wither (as herbage)
KJV: be ashamed, clean, be confounded, (make) dry (up), (do) shame(-fully), [idiom] utterly, wither (away).

H3002.definition:
from H3001 (יָבֵשׁ);
dry
KJV: dried (away), dry.

H3003.definition:
the same as H3002 (יָבֵשׁ) (also יָבֵישׁ; often with the addition of H1568 (גִּלְעָד), i.e. Jabesh of Gilad);
Jobesh, the name of an Israelite and of a place in Palestine
KJV: Jobesh (-Gilead).

H3004.definition:
from H3001 (יָבֵשׁ);
dry ground
KJV: dry (ground, land).

H3005.definition:
from the same as H1314 (בֶּשֶׂם); fragrant;
Jibsam, an Israelite
KJV: Jibsam.

H3006.definition:
a variation of H3004 (יַבָּשָׁה);
dry ground
KJV: dry land.

H3007.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3006 (יַבֶּשֶׁת);
dry land
KJV: earth.

H3008.definition:
from H1350 (גָּאַל); avenger;
Jigal, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Igal, Igeal.

H3009.definition:
a primitive root;
to dig or plow
KJV: husbandman.

H3010.definition:
from H3009 (יָגַב);
a plowed field
KJV: field.

H3011.definition:
feminine from H1361 (גָּבַהּ); hillock;
Jogbehah, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Jogbehah.

H3012.definition:
from H1431 (גָּדַל) and H3050 (יָהּ); magnified of Jah;
Jigdaljah, an Israelite
KJV: Igdaliah.

H3013.definition:
a primitive root;
to grieve
KJV: afflict, cause grief, grieve, sorrowful, vex.

H3014.definition:
a primitive root (probably rather the same as H3013 (יָגָה) through the common idea of dissatisfaction);
to push away
KJV: be removed.

H3015.definition:
from H3013 (יָגָה);
affliction
KJV: grief, sorrow.

H3016.definition:
from H3025 (יָגֹר);
fearful
KJV: afraid, fearest.

H3017.definition:
probably from H1481 (גּוּר); a lodging;
Jagur, a place in Palestine
KJV: Jagur.

H3018.definition:
from H3021 (יָגַע);
toil; hence, a work, produce, property (as the result of labor)
KJV: labour, work.

H3020.definition:
from H1540 (גָּלָה); exiled;
Jogli, an Israelite
KJV: Jogli.

H3021.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to gasp; hence, to be exhausted, to tire, to toil
KJV: faint, (make to) labour, (be) weary.

H3022.definition:
from H3021 (יָגַע);
earnings (as the product of toil)
KJV: that which he laboured for.

H3023.definition:
from H3021 (יָגַע);
tired; hence (transitive) tiresome
KJV: full of labour, weary.

H3024.definition:
feminine of H3019 (יָגִיעַ);
fatigue
KJV: weariness.

H3025.definition:
a primitive root;
to fear
KJV: be afraid, fear.

H3026.definition:
(Aramaic) from a word derived from an unused root (meaning to gather) and a derivation of a root corresponding to H7717 (שָׂהֵד); heap of the testimony;
Jegar-Sahadutha, a cairn East of the Jordan
KJV: Jegar-Sahadutha.

H3028.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3027 (יָד)
{a hand (the open one (indicating power, means, direction, etc.)}
KJV: hand, power.

H3029.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3034 (יָדָה);
to praise
KJV: (give) thank(-s).

H3030.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Jidalah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Idalah.

H3031.definition:
from the same as H1706 (דְּבַשׁ); perhaps honeyed;
Jidbash, an Israelite
KJV: Idbash.

H3033.definition:
from H3039 (יְדִיד);
properly, affection; concretely, a darling object
KJV: dearly beloved.

H3034.definition:
a primitive root; used only as denominative from H3027 (יָד); literally, to use (i.e. hold out) the hand;
physically, to throw (a stone, an arrow) at or away; especially to revere or worship (with extended hands); intensively, to bemoan (by wringing the hands)
KJV: cast (out), (make) confess(-ion), praise, shoot, (give) thank(-ful, -s, -sgiving).

H3035.definition:
from H3034 (יָדָה); praised;
Jiddo, an Israelite
KJV: Iddo.

H3036.definition:
from H3034 (יָדָה); thankful;
Jadon, an Israelite
KJV: Jadon.

H3037.definition:
from H3045 (יָדַע); knowing;
Jaddua, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Jaddua.

H3038.definition:
or יְדֻתוּן; or יְדִיתוּן; probably from H3034 (יָדָה); laudatory;
Jeduthun, an Israelite
KJV: Jeduthun.

H3039.definition:
from the same as H1730 (דּוֹד);
loved
KJV: amiable, (well-) beloved, loves.

H3040.definition:
feminine of H3039 (יְדִיד); beloved;
Jedidah, an Israelitess
KJV: Jedidah.

H3041.definition:
from H3039 (יְדִיד) and H3050 (יָהּ); beloved of Jah;
Jedidejah, a name of Solomon
KJV: Jedidiah.

H3042.definition:
from H3034 (יָדָה) and H3050 (יָהּ); praised of Jah;
Jedajah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Jedaiah.

H3043.definition:
from H3045 (יָדַע) and H410 (אֵל); knowing God;
Jediael, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Jediael.

H3044.definition:
from H1811 (דָּלַף); tearful;
Jidlaph, a Mesopotamian
KJV: Jidlaph.

H3045.definition:
a primitive root;
to know (properly, to ascertain by seeing); used in a great variety of senses, figuratively, literally, euphemistically and inferentially (including observation, care, recognition; and causatively, instruction, designation, punishment, etc.)
KJV: acknowledge, acquaintance(-ted with), advise, answer, appoint, assuredly, be aware, (un-) awares, can(-not), certainly, comprehend, consider, [idiom] could they, cunning, declare, be diligent, (can, cause to) discern, discover, endued with, familiar friend, famous, feel, can have, be (ig-) norant, instruct, kinsfolk, kinsman, (cause to let, make) know, (come to give, have, take) knowledge, have (knowledge), (be, make, make to be, make self) known, [phrase] be learned, [phrase] lie by man, mark, perceive, privy to, [idiom] prognosticator, regard, have respect, skilful, shew, can (man of) skill, be sure, of a surety, teach, (can) tell, understand, have (understanding), [idiom] will be, wist, wit, wot.

H3046.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3045 (יָדַע)
{to know (properly, to ascertain by seeing); used in a great variety of senses, figuratively, literally, euphemistically and inferentially (including observation, care, recognition; and causatively, instruction, designation, punishment, etc.)}
KJV: certify, know, make known, teach.

H3047.definition:
from H3045 (יָדַע); knowing;
Jada, an Israelite
KJV: Jada.

H3048.definition:
from H3045 (יָדַע) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has known;
Jedajah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Jedaiah.

H3049.definition:
from H3045 (יָדַע);
properly, a knowing one; specifically, a conjurer; (by impl) a ghost
KJV: wizard.

H3050.definition:
contraction for H3068 (יְהֹוָה), and meaning the same;
Jah, the sacred name
KJV: Jah, the Lord, most vehement. Compare names in '-iah,' '-jah.'

H3051.definition:
a primitive root;
to give (whether literal or figurative); generally, to put; imperatively (reflexive) come
KJV: ascribe, bring, come on, give, go, set, take.

H3052.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3051 (יָהַב)
{to give (whether literal or figurative); generally, to put; imperatively (reflexive) come}
KJV: deliver, give, lay, [phrase] prolong, pay, yield.

H3053.definition:
from H3051 (יָהַב);
properly, what is given (by Providence), i.e. a lot
KJV: burden.

H3054.definition:
denominative from a form corresponding to H3061 (יְהוּד)lemma יְהיּד yod, corrected to יְהוּד;
to Judaize, i.e. become Jewish
KJV: become Jews.

H3055.definition:
a briefer form of one corresponding to H3061 (יְהוּד)lemma יְהיּד yod, corrected to יְהוּד;
Jehud, a place in Palestine
KJV: Jehud.

H3056.definition:
perhaps from a form corresponding to H3061 (יְהוּד)lemma יְהיּד yod, corrected to יְהוּד; Judaistic;
Jehdai, an Israelite
KJV: Jehdai.

H3057.definition:
feminine of H3064 (יְהוּדִי);
Jehudijah, a Jewess
KJV: Jehudijah.

H3058.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H1931 (הוּא); Jehovah (is) He;
Jehu, the name of five Israelites
KJV: Jehu.

H3059.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H270 (אָחַז); Jehovah-seized;
Jehoachaz, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Jehoahaz. Compare H3099 (יוֹאָחָז).

H3060.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and (perhaps) H784 (אֵשׁ); Jehovah-fired;
Jehoash, the name of two Israelite kings
KJV: Jehoash. Compare H3101 (יוֹאָשׁ).

H3061.definition:
(Aramaic) contracted from a form corresponding to H3063 (יְהוּדָה);
properly, Judah, hence, Judaea
KJV: Jewry, Judah, Judea.

H3062.definition:
(Aramaic) patrial from H3061 (יְהוּד)lemma יְהיּד yod, corrected to יְהוּד;
a Jehudaite (or Judaite), i.e. Jew
KJV: Jew.

H3063.definition:
from H3034 (יָדָה); celebrated;
Jehudah (or Judah), the name of five Israelites; also of the tribe descended from the first, and of its territory
KJV: Judah.

H3064.definition:
patronymically from H3063 (יְהוּדָה);
a Jehudite (i.e. Judaite or Jew), or descendant of Jehudah (i.e. Judah)
KJV: Jew.

H3065.definition:
the same as H3064 (יְהוּדִי);
Jehudi, an Israelite
KJV: Jehudi.

H3066.definition:
feminine of H3064 (יְהוּדִי);
the Jewish (used adverbially) language
KJV: in the Jews' language.

H3067.definition:
the same as H3066 (יְהוּדִית); Jewess;
Jehudith, a Canaanitess
KJV: Judith.

H3068.definition:
from H1961 (הָיָה); (the) self-Existent or Eternal;
Jehovah, Jewish national name of God
KJV: Jehovah, the Lord. Compare H3050 (יָהּ), H3069 (יְהֹוִה).

H3069.definition:
a variation of H3068 (יְהֹוָה) (used after H136 (אֲדֹנָי), and pronounced by Jews as H430 (אֱלֹהִים), in order to prevent the repetition of the same sound, since they elsewhere pronounce H3068 (יְהֹוָה) as H136 (אֲדֹנָי))
{YHWH}
KJV: God.

H3070.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H7200 (רָאָה); Jehovah will see (to it);
Jehovah-Jireh, a symbolical name for Mount Moriah
KJV: Jehovah-jireh.

H3071.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H5251 (נֵס) with the prononimal suffix; Jehovah (is) my banner;
Jehovah-Nissi, a symbolical name of an altar in the Desert
KJV: Jehovah-nissi.

H3072.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H6664 (צֶדֶק) with pronominal suffix; Jehovah (is) our right;
Jehovah-Tsidkenu, a symbolical epithet of the Messiah and of Jerusalem
KJV: the Lord our righteousness.

H3073.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H7965 (שָׁלוֹם); Jehovah (is) peace;
Jehovah-Shalom, a symbolical name of an altar in Palestine
KJV: Jehovah-shalom.

H3074.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H8033 (שָׁם) with directive enclitic; Jehovah (is) thither;
Jehovah-Shammah, a symbolic title of Jerusalem
KJV: Jehovahshammah.

H3075.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H2064 (זָבַד); Jehovah-endowed;
Jehozabad, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Jehozabad. Compare H3107 (יוֹזָבָד).

H3076.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H2603 (חָנַן); Jehovah-favored;
Jehochanan, the name of eight Israelites
KJV: Jehohanan, Johanan. Compare H3110 (יוֹחָנָן).

H3077.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H3045 (יָדַע); Jehovah-known;
Jehojada, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Jehoiada. Compare H3111 (יוֹיָדָע).

H3078.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H3559 (כּוּן); Jehovah will establish;
Jehojakin, a Jewish king
KJV: Jehoiachin. Compare H3112 (יוֹיָכִין).

H3079.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) abbreviated and H6965 (קוּם); Jehovah will raise;
Jehojakim, a Jewish king
KJV: Jehoiakim. Compare H3113 (יוֹיָקִים).

H3080.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H7378 (רִיב); Jehovah will contend;
Jehojarib, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Jehoiarib. Compare H3114 (יוֹיָרִיב).

H3081.definition:
from H3201 (יָכֹל); potent;
Jehukal, an Israelite
KJV: Jehucal. Compare H3116 (יוּכַל).

H3082.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H5068 (נָדַב); Jehovah-largessed;
Jehonadab, the name of an Israelite and of an Arab
KJV: Jehonadab, Jonadab. Compare H3122 (יוֹנָדָב).

H3083.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H5414 (נָתַן); Jehovah-given;
Jehonathan, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Jonathan. Compare H3129 (יוֹנָתָן).

H3084.definition:
a fuller form of H3130 (יוֹסֵף);
Jehoseph (i.e. Joseph), a son of Jacob
KJV: Joseph.

H3085.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H5710 (עָדָה); Jehovah-adorned;
Jehoaddah, an Israelite
KJV: Jehoada.

H3086.definition:
or יְהוֹעַדָּן; from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H5727 (עָדַן); Jehovahpleased;
Jehoaddin or Jehoaddan, an Israelitess
KJV: Jehoaddan.

H3087.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H6663 (צָדַק); Jehovah-righted;
Jehotsadak, an Israelite
KJV: Jehozadek, Josedech. Compare H3136 (יוֹצָדָק).

H3088.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H7311 (רוּם); Jehovah-raised;
Jehoram, the name of a Syrian and of three Israelites
KJV: Jehoram, Joram. Compare H3141 (יוֹרָם).

H3089.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H7650 (שָׁבַע); Jehovah-sworn;
Jehosheba, an Israelitess
KJV: Jehosheba. Compare H3090 (יְהוֹשַׁבְעַת).

H3090.definition:
a form of H3089 (יְהוֹשֶׁבַע);
Jehoshabath, an Israelitess
KJV: Jehoshabeath.

H3091.definition:
or יְהוֹשֻׁעַ; from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H3467 (יָשַׁע); Jehovah-saved;
Jehoshua (i.e. Joshua), the Jewish leader
KJV: Jehoshua, Jehoshuah, Joshua. Compare H1954 (הוֹשֵׁעַ), H3442 (יֵשׁוּעַ).

H3092.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H8199 (שָׁפַט); Jehovah-judged;
Jehoshaphat, the name of six Israelites; also of a valley near Jerusalem
KJV: Jehoshaphat. Compare H3146 (יוֹשָׁפָט).

H3093.definition:
probably from the same as H2022 (הַר);
elated; hence, arrogant
KJV: haughty, proud.

H3094.definition:
from H1984 (הָלַל) and H410 (אֵל); praising God;
Jehallelel, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Jehalellel, Jehalelel.

H3095.definition:
from H1986 (הָלַם) (in the sense of hardness);
a precious stone, probably onyx
KJV: diamond.

H3096.definition:
or יַהְצָה; or (feminine) יַהְצָה; from an unused root meaning to stamp; perhaps threshing-floor;
Jahats or Jahtsah, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Jahaz, Jahazah, Jahzah.

H3097.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H1 (אָב); Jehovah-fathered;
Joab, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Joab.

H3098.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H251 (אָח); Jehovahbrothered;
Joach, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Joah.

H3099.definition:
a form of H3059 (יְהוֹאָחָז);
Joachaz, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Jehoahaz, Joahaz.
